# Synthetic footprints for the cos(dec) footprint test.
#
# Every footprint is 1 deg x 1 deg on the sky (except the ears), so its
# area and its east-west extent must not depend on declination.
# Order matters: test_cosdec_footprint.f95 indexes these entries.
#
# 1-5: rectangles at Dec 0, +30, +60, -60, +75
rect 1.0 1.0  30.0   0.0 2456391.5 1.0 500 cosdec.eff
rect 1.0 1.0  60.0  30.0 2456391.5 1.0 500 cosdec.eff
rect 1.0 1.0  90.0  60.0 2456391.5 1.0 500 cosdec.eff
rect 1.0 1.0 120.0 -60.0 2456391.5 1.0 500 cosdec.eff
rect 1.0 1.0 150.0  75.0 2456391.5 1.0 500 cosdec.eff
#
# 6: rectangle straddling RA = 0
rect 1.0 1.0   0.1  30.0 2456391.5 1.0 500 cosdec.eff
#
# 7: MegaPrime "ears" footprint
ears 200.0 60.0 2456391.5 1.0 500 cosdec.eff
#
# 8: polygon of tangent-plane offsets [deg], 1 deg square
poly 4 250.0 60.0 2456391.5 1.0 500 cosdec.eff
-0.5 -0.5
-0.5  0.5
 0.5  0.5
 0.5 -0.5
#
# 9: 8 deg x 1 deg strip of fields tiled along Dec = 60
rect 8.0 1.0 300.0 60.0 2456391.5 1.0 500 cosdec.eff
#
# 10: slanted 7 deg block, shaped like OSSOS 2013AE
poly 4 213.87 -12.54 2456391.5 1.0 500 cosdec.eff
-3.5 -0.434889
-3.5  2.565111
 3.5  0.473417
 3.5 -2.526583
